# Git hooks must keep LF endings even on Windows checkouts.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf rewrites `.githooks/pre-commit` to CRLF on
# checkout, and the shebang line becomes "#!/bin/sh\r" -- the shell then looks
# for an interpreter literally named "sh\r" and every commit dies with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory". The hook would appear installed
# and simply never work.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
